First Author: Agasthi
Title: Machine learning helps predict long-term mortality and graft failure in patients undergoing heart transplant
Source number: 2  ￼

Very short summary: This retrospective study used the ISHLT registry to develop a gradient-boosted machine model for predicting 5-year mortality and 5-year graft failure after orthotopic heart transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) the final cohort included 15,236 adult heart transplant recipients; (2) the model used 87 variables selected from an initial 342; (3) 5-year mortality was 27.3% and 5-year graft failure was 28.1%; (4) the model achieved AUC 0.717 for 5-year mortality and 0.716 for 5-year graft failure; and (5) the most influential predictors were hospital length of stay, recipient age, donor age, recipient and donor BMI, and ischemic time, with Figure 2 showing better graft-failure prediction in recipients older than 60 years and better mortality prediction when ischemic time exceeded 4 hours.  ￼  ￼

