	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper describes a retrospective registry cohort and states that endpoints were evaluated “using the gradient-boosted machine (GBM) algorithm.” The dataset was split into “training cohort” 80% and “validation cohort” 20%, with “tenfold cross-validation repeated 5 times” used within training to tune hyperparameters. Feature selection was automated by removing variables with >50% missingness and near-zero variance, with recoding of sparse categories, resulting in 87 variables for modeling. No explicit clinical-rule comparator was tested in the main analysis.  ￼  ￼

